+# Source attribution and reuse
+
+## CBETA
+
+These short research excerpts derive from CBETA XML TEI P5, Taishō T0251, T1558 and T1614, at commit `dbdea41071e1e260ad84b72faefd4587333cf76d`. Each source’s complete XML header accompanies the excerpts as `T0251-source-header.xml`, `T1558-source-header.xml` or `T1614-source-header.xml`. File hashes, pinned source URLs and original publication dates are recorded in `claims.json`.
+
+CBETA data remain subject to [CBETA’s source terms](https://cbeta.org/copyright), including attribution, noncommercial use and applicable share-alike requirements. Their general license is [CC BY-NC-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/), with source-specific exceptions retained. Our presentation removes line-breaking whitespace and markup but preserves the quoted reading; it does not replace the source edition.
+
+## Chinese WordNet
+
+The 27 short native-sense records retain the original identifiers and definitions from CWN image `v.2022.08.01`. This is an exact-lemma research excerpt for 心, 意 and 識. The upstream [CwnGraph repository](https://github.com/lopentu/CwnGraph), its manifest and the image hash are recorded in `cwn-native.json`. Original resource terms remain applicable; no independent relicensing of the dictionary is asserted. Proposed historical mappings are the project’s annotations and remain pending review.
+
+## Sanskrit transcription
+
+Brief quotations are taken from the [NTU Buddhist Digital Library transcription](https://buddhism.lib.ntu.edu.tw/FULLTEXT/mukherjee/articles/html/sk-heart.htm), retrieved 7 September 2026. The raw file hash and decoding note are retained. The quotation is a hosted transcription, not a newly established critical edition or a demonstrated direct translation source.
+
+## Annotation status
+
+All 16 claims are machine-prepared proposals. Local source checking does not imply expert endorsement. Reusers must retain the distinction among source checks, interpretation, mapping proposals and expert adjudication.
